Records the decisions behind the three previous commits (tracer audit
finding 7): ridge centring for even-width strokes, the round-bend guard,
one rebuilt corner per bend, the tip walk reading between pixel centres,
and the zero join gap. Also records why the 4 px maxDev values left on
the 8 px strokes are the end convention (the traced line runs to the end
of the ink, half a stroke width past the true centreline's end), with the
measurements and the known limits left for later.

