+## ADR-394 - Centerline centres strokes on the sub-pixel ridge and keeps drawn curves round (2026-09-25)
+
+**Status:** Accepted. | **Date:** 2026-09-25
+
+### Context
+
+The 2026-09-24 tracer audit (finding 7) measured Centerline on 21 synthetic strokes with known
+centrelines: a mean distance of 0.25 px from the true centre, ahead of AutoTrace, with two errors.
+
+- **Rounded bends in thick strokes become sharp corners.** `centerline/sharpen-bends.ts` rebuilds a
+  bend as the corner its two straight legs point at, and keeps only roundings of about two stroke
+  radii or more. Thinning cuts inside a drawn corner and follows a rounded bend, and in a thick
+  stroke both leave a short, concentrated turn between straight legs, so the shape gates cannot
+  tell them apart. On the new base (85ee406) the 8 px
+  wave's rounded bottoms turned into V shapes, leaving the true centre up to 2.24 px from the trace.
+- **Strokes an even number of pixels wide sit 0.5 px off centre.** The ridge of the exact distance
+  transform (Felzenszwalb and Huttenlocher) lies between two pixel centres there. Distance-ordered
+  homotopic thinning (Pudney) keeps whole pixels, so the skeleton takes one of the two.
+
+Three more things came up while fixing these:
+
+- **The tip walk turned off the axis of round caps.** `extendTip` walks from the skeleton's end to
+  the ink tip and breaks ties by the radius of the nearest pixel. That radius jumps a whole lattice
+  step between neighbouring candidates and turned the walk 22.5° off a round cap's axis. Centring
+  changed the chain ends and pushed the in-repo regression bar's 9 px arc from 0.79 px to 1.25 px of
+  maximum deviation, over its 1 px limit.
+- **A rebuilt corner could be built again.** After a rebuild the sharpener's scan moves to the next
+  point along the chain. That point's window can take in the new corner, whose own leg is straight,
+  so the candidate passes every gate and builds a second corner beside the first from a tangent read
+  further down the other leg. The distance rule meant to stop this (2.5 px) misses when the second
+  corner lands further away. Centring straightens the legs, so it happened more: on a 12 px stroke's
+  45° corner the second corner stood 3 px past the first and 1.5 px off the pen's path.
+- **The separate-end gap bridge at zero.** WORKFLOW says "Zero disables that gap bridge", and a
+  trace-dialog control for the gap is being added in a separate change. `bridgeNearbyEnds` returns
+  before pairing any ends when the gap is zero or less, so the statement holds.
+
+### Decision
+
+1. **Centre chains on the sub-pixel ridge** (`centerline/ridge-centering.ts`, run after junction
+   condensation and before assembly). For each chain point that sits on a pixel centre, read the
+   distance field one pixel to either side along the chain's normal (taken from the points two
+   either side), with bilinear reads (`interpolatedRadius`). Fit a tent through the three values:
+   two lines of equal and opposite slope, which is the shape of the distance to the nearer edge
+   across a straight band. Move the point to the tent's apex, at most half a pixel. Junction nodes
+   and former junctions (`seamJunctions`) stay where they are, because pairing, seam repair and the
+   attachment pins find them by position. An open chain's own end moves with its endpoint node.
+2. **Keep a rounded bend round in centreline strokes** (`centerline/round-bend-guard.ts`, enabled
+   by `sharpenChainBends(..., { keepRoundedBends: true })` from `stroke-chains.ts` only). Before
+   accepting a rebuilt corner, compare the ink radius at the rebuilt vertex with the legs' radius:
+   the smaller of the two medians read on each leg just outside the bend. The ink the vertex lost
+   says how far it stands off the pen's path. The rest of its offset from the chain is how far the
+   chain stands off. Rebuild only when the loss is at most max(0.6 px, half the offset), which is
+   when the vertex is the nearer of the two.
+3. **Build one corner per bend in centreline strokes** (`oneCornerPerBend: true`, also from
+   `stroke-chains.ts` only). A candidate is skipped when the points its vertex would be built from,
+   the window it replaces and the 3 px tangent chords either side, include a corner already rebuilt
+   on the chain. The contour tracer passes neither option, so outlines are unchanged.
+4. **Read the ridge between pixel centres in the tip walk**: its tie-break uses
+   `interpolatedRadius` instead of the nearest pixel's radius.
+5. **The gap bridge's zero stays as it is.** A unit test now pins that a gap of zero or less
+   bridges no ends, even touching, aligned ones.
+
+### Consequences
+
+- 21-stroke centreline corpus from the audit, new base against this change: mean distance from the
+  true centre 0.254 to 0.102 px; mean 95th percentile 0.43 to 0.20 px; share of the true centreline
+  covered 99.84% to 100%; fragment counts unchanged. Every stroke improves or holds its mean except
+  cross-w4 (0.093 to 0.186 px). Its tip now ends 0.71 px off the axis instead of 1.28 px, which
+  changes the kink next to a 248 px chord. The output spline, shared with the contour tracer, then
+  bows that chord by up to its 0.45 px cap.
+- The 8 px wave's largest gap falls from 2.24 to 0.15 px. Centring alone or the guard alone also
+  removes the V shapes.
+- The largest deviation of every open stroke in that corpus sits at a stroke end. The true
+  centreline stops where the pen stopped; the traced line runs on to the end of the ink, half a
+  stroke width further, and the bench counts that reach. The 8 px corner and tee read 4.03 px
+  because their tips also sat 0.5 px off the axis, and now read 4.00 px. What remains across the
+  axis at a tip comes from the tip walk's 16 compass directions: the 8 px diagonal runs 9.3° from
+  the nearest one, and its tips end 0.65 and 0.83 px off the axis (4 px × sin 9.3° is 0.65 px).
+- A 290-bend corpus (3-12 px strokes, 45-150° turns, sharp, mitred and filleted paths; mean of each
+  bend's local maximum error): 1.25 to 0.57 px. 235 bends improve by more than 0.1 px and 20 get
+  worse, by at most 0.79 px, 14 of them at 3-4 px widths. At those widths the ink cannot reliably
+  tell a fillet of about one stroke radius from a drawn corner. The guard alone improves 88 bends
+  and worsens one. The one-corner rule changes five bends, all for the better (a 12 px stroke's 45°
+  corners from 1.5-1.8 px to 0.6-0.7 px), and no stroke of the 21-stroke corpus.
+- The in-repo regression bar: maximum deviation 0.69 to 0.19 px for h-stroke, l-corner and cross,
+  and 0.79 to 0.10 px for the arc.
+- The contour presets (Line Art, Smooth, Sharp, Edge Detection) give identical output, timing field
+  aside: 48 of 48 audit corpus traces, and all 8 traces of the dragon and Arch House logo.
+- Dragon (`centerline-stress-test-20260909.png`): 2,518 to 2,522 paths, 66,690 to 65,986 vertices;
+  share of traced length on ink 0.820 to 0.835. Four more paths come from pairs of ends 2-3 px apart
+  that centring moves across the bridge's reach. Logo (`arch-house-langebaan-source.png`): 74 paths
+  either way, 2,552 to 2,665 vertices; the traced line's radius relative to the local ridge rises
+  from 0.906 to 0.917. On the two images the one-corner rule leaves out 36 of 752 rebuilt corners;
+  corners standing within 12 px of an earlier one fall from 43 to 10. Centring costs about 68 ms on
+  the dragon's 98,000 chain points.
+- The guard's half is the break-even point, not a tuned value. On the bend corpus, where rebuilding
+  helped, the vertex lost at most 0.21 of its offset (4-12 px strokes). Where it did not help, the
+  vertex lost a median 0.54-0.86. A lower cut of 0.35 caught more curves in that corpus but rounded
+  the pointed tops of the logo's capital A and N, so it was rejected.
+- Known limits, unchanged here: the tip walk still steps in 16 compass directions; the output
+  spline can bow a long chord next to a kinked end segment by up to its cap; flat-ended bars end
+  1/6 px off, at the junction centroid; 150° hairpins in thick strokes end up to half a stroke
+  width short; one tip of the 8 px X ends 1.41 px off its axis (1.86 px before).
+- Tests: `ridge-centering.test.ts` (tent apex, even and odd widths, fixed junctions, a 4 px ring
+  within 0.2 px of its centre circle), `round-bend-guard.test.ts` (a 12 px stroke's 9 px fillet
+  stays round, the same stroke's drawn corner is rebuilt, the option is off unless asked for),
+  `corner-rebuilt-once.test.ts` (a 12 px stroke's 45° corner is rebuilt once, within 1 px of the
+  pen's path), `tip-extension.test.ts` (the arc's round caps end within 0.5 px of their axes), and
+  `gap-distance.test.ts` (zero gap).
+
